  "decisiveFinding": "Both direct64 raw and common-palette/binary-alpha codec remain HELD,0/1 useful blink clips each. A small face/eye pixel change is visible under scrutiny, but not an unambiguous closed-eye cue during the normal100ms interval. The codec is structurally cleaner without resolving the semantic failure.",
  "continuity": "Same broad bird identity, scale and quiet stance are retained. Small feather/toe changes do not alone cause rejection; exact pixel equality and numeric bounds are not semantic gates. No root translation/bob, eye paint, pose fit, snap, crop or time extension is used by this review.",
  "diagnosticLimits": "Eye ROI dark-pixel coordinates are not tracked eyelid masks; some may be beak/head. Matching27x18 opaque bounds and small foot ROI differences do not prove physical support. Positive alpha is not pressure or grip. The normal-size eye ambiguity, rather than numeric mismatches, is the held reason.",
